<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perthshire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as County of Perth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Perthshire is a historic county of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, stretching from the Highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atholl">Atholl</a> and Breadalbane to the lowland valley of the Tay. It contains Scone, where Scottish kings were inaugurated, and the early church centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkeld">Dunkeld</a>, and in the Pictish period it lay at the heart of the over-kingship that grew into the kingdom of Alba. Its county town is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perth">Perth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perthshire.jpg" alt="Perthshire" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brythones, derivative of Visitor from Wikishire · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perthshire_County.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
